    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Honduras left the Central American federation in 1838; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#marco-aurelio-soto">Marco Aurelio Soto</a> made Tegucigalpa its permanent capital in 1880.</li><li>American fruit companies dominated its north coast from the 1900s, and O. Henry coined ‘banana republic’ with Honduras in mind.</li><li>Dictatorship, military rule, the 1969 Football War, Contra bases and the 2009 coup have marked its modern history.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 1911 the banana <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#magnates">magnate</a> Samuel Zemurray financed an invasion of Honduras that restored the former president Manuel Bonilla, who rewarded him with land concessions.</p></aside>
    </section>

